-- Hotfix (WO-E209): `print` wants a `Text` -- a heap-string pointer,
-- .wob kind WO_K_TEXT -- and a bare Int literal is a WO_K_SCALAR
-- register holding a raw int64 (docs/plan/oop-vm/08-builtin-surface.md's
-- `print(t)` row). Before this check existed, this compiled clean and
-- segfaulted `wovm`: the VM's `str_check` (runtime/src/vm.c) dereferences
-- whatever register it's handed as a `wo_str*` with no runtime tag to
-- check first, so the literal `7` was a wild pointer read. The exact
-- repro that motivated wiring this diagnostic up.
fn main() {
  print(7)
}
